cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."

authors:
  - family-names: Zhu
    given-names: Boyan

doi: ""

title: "kestrel-repro: Evidence-Driven Deep Learning Paper Reproduction Plugin for Cursor"

version: "0.2.0"

repository-code: "https://github.com/carlkestrel/kestrel-repro"
url: "https://github.com/carlkestrel/kestrel-repro"

abstract: >-
  kestrel-repro is a Cursor IDE plugin that provides a structured, evidence-first
  workflow for reproducing deep learning papers from their official GitHub
  repositories. It enforces six staged gates (paper audit, preflight, short-loop,
  parity testing, full training, and evidence verification) and produces machine-readable
  evidence chains for every claimed result. Designed for any PyTorch-based paper,
  with specialized support for point cloud processing papers (KPConv, PointNet++,
  DGCNN, etc.) and datasets (S3DIS, ScanNet, SemanticKITTI).

keywords:
  - deep-learning
  - paper-reproduction
  - reproducibility
  - pytorch
  - point-cloud
  - evidence-chain
  - cursor-ide
  - research-automation
  - benchmark
  - auditing

